Alternative Merge List
    Takes two lists as input.
    Merges them by picking elements alternately from each list.
    Handles cases where lists are of unequal lengths.
    Returns or prints the merged list.


Pair Sum Finder
    Accepts a list of numbers and a target sum.
    Finds all unique pairs whose sum equals the target.
    Avoids duplicate pair outputs.
    Displays the found pairs to the user.


Pyramid
    Takes the number of rows as input from the user.
    Generates a pyramid shape using symbols (e.g., *).
    Uses loops to manage spacing and alignment.
    Displays the pyramid neatly in the console.


Secret Message
    Takes a message from the user.
    Encodes the message using a custom transformation logic.
    Can decode back to the original message if needed.
    Demonstrates string manipulation with lists/tuples.


Tuple Based
Shows creation and usage of tuples in Python.
Demonstrates tuple indexing, slicing, and unpacking.
Includes examples of nested tuples.
Highlights immutability and when to use tuples over lists.